cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ParliamentariansTN: a relational dataset of Tunisian parliamentarians, 1956-present"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it and state which chamber-terms your analysis covers."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Hammami
    given-names: Mohamed Dhia
    affiliation: Syracuse University
abstract: >-
  A relational dataset of Tunisian parliamentarians spanning nineteen
  chamber-terms from the 1956 National Constituent Assembly to the sitting
  Assembly of the Representatives of the People. It records persons separately
  from mandates, stores party, bloc, committee and career affiliations as dated
  spells, and carries cell-level provenance linking every value to a source and
  a retrieval date. Person-level coverage is complete for the 1956 Constituent
  Assembly, the 2011-2014 National Constituent Assembly, the 2014-2019 and
  2019-2021 Assemblies of the Representatives of the People and the chamber
  elected in 2023, giving a continuous panel across the democratic period; the
  eleven chambers of the single-party era (1959-2011) are present as
  institutional frame only. Derived network files support committee
  co-membership, bloc co-membership, shared-constituency, shared-organisation and
  written-question co-signature analyses.
keywords:
  - Tunisia
  - legislative politics
  - parliamentary elites
  - social network analysis
  - elite circulation
  - authoritarianism
  - democratization
  - Middle East and North Africa
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MedDhia/ParliamentariansTN"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-27"
